`F_j=[w^j]_+` are monic of degree `j`, so triangularity gives a unique
expansion

```text
g=sum_(j=0)^n h_j F_j,       h_n=1.                  (2.1)
```

Define the negative tail by

```text
H(w)-g(z(w))=sum_(ell>=1) r_ell w^-ell,
H(T)=sum_(j=0)^n h_j T^j.                            (2.2)
```

For

```text
D=f_x g_z-f_z g_x,
```

